#X text 430 42 Note on ratio: Harmonic spectra occur when the ratio of carrier to modulator frequency is rational \; The fundamental frequency is GCD(C \, M) The greatest frequency that can be multiplied to get C \, M \, and any side band (C +|- nM) \; If C/M = N1/N2 where N1 \, and N2 are coprime integers \, then the harmonic numbers of the bands are given by k = N1 +|- nN2 - That makes N1 the start harmonic \, and N2 the distance between harmonics. \; Number of side bands heard ~ I + 1 \, so you may not always hear f0. - Calculating C and M from N1 \, N2 and f0 => C = f0*N1 \, M = f0*N2 \, making their GCD f0 and their ratio N1/N2, f 28;
#X floatatom 195 469 10 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X floatatom 289 469 11 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X floatatom 138 468 5 0 0 0 - - - 0;
#X text 459 396 Preserving the tonic requires more than just coprime N1 \, N2. The true constraint is that there exists an integer n such that N1 + nN2 = 1 If not \, another harmonic becomes the apparent fundamental. Not to mention the fundamental created from the effects of aliasing. I will one day solve this problem., f 21;
